# Home base

`cfwest86/cfwest86` is the starting repository for new chats. It stores routing rules, skills, and `docs/repos.md`.

`README.md` is the public GitHub profile. Keep that profile text. Put hub documentation in `docs/`.

Before doing any work:

1. Read `docs/repos.md`.
2. Hub work (rules, skills, catalog, routing) happens in this repository.
3. When a listed repository matches, stop. Name it, link it, and give a prompt to paste into a new chat opened on that repository. Follow the `route-chat` skill.
4. When no repository matches, follow the `propose-new-repo` skill. Wait for an explicit yes before treating a new repository as real.
5. Keep project code, notebooks, and datasets in the project repository.
6. Keep secrets, tokens, and private data out of this public repository.
